STAR/FOLD native media previews

STAR/KIT dynamically links FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), including
libavcodec, libavformat, libavutil, libavfilter, libswscale and libswresample.
The media player is native Rust; FFmpeg supplies codecs and conversion.

Most FFmpeg code is licensed under LGPL 2.1 or later; the license text is in
LICENSES/ffmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt. FFmpeg builds enabling GPL components, including
libx264 used for the SSH H.264 preview, are governed by the corresponding GPL
terms. Dynamically linked binary distributions inherit the linked build's
applicable terms. Application sources remain available in this repository.

Nix and Arch use their distribution's FFmpeg. AppImages bundle Debian's shared
libraries in usr/lib, replaceable with compatible libraries without rebuilding
STAR/FOLD. macOS archives require Homebrew FFmpeg. Sources for these libraries
are available from https://ffmpeg.org/download.html and the supplying
package distribution. See FFmpeg's LICENSE.md for component-specific terms.
